From fbffe03bc3554ed746558ab72fdba26238a3f379 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:13:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: an owner's pre-session
 capsule_observation_missing refusal books a preadmission proof

worker-3 2026-11-13 07:21-08:25Z: the owner refused kanban.run for t_01a1d1197fa00599 with
capsule_observation_missing (session_kanban.run_task raises it before creating any session) six
times; the submitter booked each as a plain exit 1 with no proof, so the runs were counted crashes
(triage) and hermes-core-wt-land could not tell them from an agent turn (review independence refused).

The refusal is the owner's own transport state, like storage_unavailable: the worker client now asks
again before admission and, when the owner keeps refusing, exits owner-unavailable (69) with
kanban_host_refusal.preadmission_proof {kind: owner_capsule_unavailable, phase: preadmission,
reason: capsule_observation_missing} on its receipt. The sweep requeues it uncounted (bounded by
NEUTRAL_STREAK_LIMIT), files the host notice, and the land gate's preadmission exemption accepts it.
An admitted claim (or a continuing one) still treats the refusal as final.
